{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4313","SecondaryAttribute":"Aqueduct in the desert Settlements in the Burning Barren desert are supplied with water through a...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Aqueduct in the desert<\/b><br><br>\n\nSettlements in the Burning Barren desert are supplied with water through a series of aqueducts. The supply to Sandharbor settlement has a leak.\n<br> <br>\nThe people in Sandharbor will die if nothing is done. There are few options for relief efforts, as there are no off-road tanker trucks and any evacuation would take too much time because both communities are remote and inaccessible. However, the control engineer can remotely switch the supply to the Midcross settlement to Sandharbor. This would provide water to Sandharbor, but kill the people in Midcross.\n<br> <br>\nIf the control engineer switches the supply from Midcross to Sandharbor, this will save 4,000 people in Sandharbor, but 40 people in Midcross will die as a result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.desertAqueduct.neutral.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.4000.n_total.4040.n_victims.40.ratio_saved_victims.100.text","QuestionID":"QID4313","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Aqueduct in the desert Settlements in the Burning Barren desert are supplied with water through a...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
