{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4869","SecondaryAttribute":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 3...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 300 people. These people will be killed by drinking poisoned water. If there are not enough volunteers, he will kill all 3,000 Whotnir by poisoning all their water wells with the same fast-acting poison.\n<br> <br>\nThe governor of the Whotnir region has selected a group of sacrificees who are trying to flee and to hide in the capital, where they will survive if they make it. The governor of the Whotnir region has located this group and can detain them to have them sacrificed, which would save the remaining Whotnir.\n<br> <br>\nIf the governor decides to detain the escapees, this will save 3,000 Whotnir, but the 300 escapees will die as result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.humanSacrifice.neutral.counterbalancing_group.2.n_saved.3000.n_total.3300.n_victims.300.ratio_saved_victims.10.text","QuestionID":"QID4869","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 3...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4533","SecondaryAttribute":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 4...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 40 people. These people will be killed by drinking poisoned water. If there are not enough volunteers, he will kill all 4,000 Whotnir by poisoning all their water wells with the same fast-acting poison.\n<br> <br>\nThe governor of the Whotnir region has selected a group of sacrificees who are trying to flee and to hide in the capital, where they will survive if they make it. The governor of the Whotnir region has located this group and can detain them to have them sacrificed, which would save the remaining Whotnir.\n<br> <br>\nIf the governor decides to detain the escapees, this will save 4,000 Whotnir, but the 40 escapees will die as result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.humanSacrifice.neutral.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.4000.n_total.4040.n_victims.40.ratio_saved_victims.100.text","QuestionID":"QID4533","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 4...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4581","SecondaryAttribute":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 4...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 40 people. These people will be killed by drinking poisoned water. If there are not enough volunteers, he will kill all 400 Whotnir by poisoning all their water wells with the same fast-acting poison.\n<br> <br>\nThe governor of the Whotnir region has selected a group of sacrificees who are trying to flee and to hide in the capital, where they will survive if they make it. The governor of the Whotnir region has located this group and can detain them to have them sacrificed, which would save the remaining Whotnir.\n<br> <br>\nIf the governor decides to detain the escapees, this will save 400 Whotnir, but the 40 escapees will die as result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.humanSacrifice.neutral.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.400.n_total.440.n_victims.40.ratio_saved_victims.10.text","QuestionID":"QID4581","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 4...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4749","SecondaryAttribute":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 4...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 40 people. These people will be killed by drinking poisoned water. If there are not enough volunteers, he will kill all 20,000 Whotnir by poisoning all their water wells with the same fast-acting poison.\n<br> <br>\nThe governor of the Whotnir region has selected a group of sacrificees who are trying to flee and to hide in the capital, where they will survive if they make it. The governor of the Whotnir region has located this group and can detain them to have them sacrificed, which would save the remaining Whotnir.\n<br> <br>\nIf the governor decides to detain the escapees, this will save 20,000 Whotnir, but the 40 escapees will die as result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.humanSacrifice.neutral.counterbalancing_group.2.n_saved.20000.n_total.20040.n_victims.40.ratio_saved_victims.500.text","QuestionID":"QID4749","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 4...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4845","SecondaryAttribute":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 4...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 40 people. These people will be killed by drinking poisoned water. If there are not enough volunteers, he will kill all 120 Whotnir by poisoning all their water wells with the same fast-acting poison.\n<br> <br>\nThe governor of the Whotnir region has selected a group of sacrificees who are trying to flee and to hide in the capital, where they will survive if they make it. The governor of the Whotnir region has located this group and can detain them to have them sacrificed, which would save the remaining Whotnir.\n<br> <br>\nIf the governor decides to detain the escapees, this will save 120 Whotnir, but the 40 escapees will die as result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.humanSacrifice.neutral.counterbalancing_group.2.n_saved.120.n_total.160.n_victims.40.ratio_saved_victims.3.text","QuestionID":"QID4845","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 4...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4437","SecondaryAttribute":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 5...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 50 people. These people will be killed by drinking poisoned water. If there are not enough volunteers, he will kill all 750 Whotnir by poisoning all their water wells with the same fast-acting poison.\n<br> <br>\nThe governor of the Whotnir region has selected a group of sacrificees who are trying to flee and to hide in the capital, where they will survive if they make it. The governor of the Whotnir region has located this group and can detain them to have them sacrificed, which would save the remaining Whotnir.\n<br> <br>\nIf the governor decides to detain the escapees, this will save 750 Whotnir, but the 50 escapees will die as result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.humanSacrifice.neutral.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.750.n_total.320.n_victims.50.ratio_saved_victims.15.text","QuestionID":"QID4437","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 5...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4677","SecondaryAttribute":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 5...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 50 people. These people will be killed by drinking poisoned water. If there are not enough volunteers, he will kill all 100 Whotnir by poisoning all their water wells with the same fast-acting poison.\n<br> <br>\nThe governor of the Whotnir region has selected a group of sacrificees who are trying to flee and to hide in the capital, where they will survive if they make it. The governor of the Whotnir region has located this group and can detain them to have them sacrificed, which would save the remaining Whotnir.\n<br> <br>\nIf the governor decides to detain the escapees, this will save 100 Whotnir, but the 50 escapees will die as result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.humanSacrifice.neutral.counterbalancing_group.2.n_saved.100.n_total.150.n_victims.50.ratio_saved_victims.2.text","QuestionID":"QID4677","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Human sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of Chirfiqa asks the Whotnir tribe to sacrifice 5...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3610","SecondaryAttribute":"In Ankradem, there are some experimenters who would like to make sure that you are still reading...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Ankradem, there are some experimenters who would like to make sure that you are still reading these scenarios. We are sure you do, but these pesky experimenters just have to insist. Please select 2,000 divided by one thousand (that is, two) for the question below to show that you have read this text.\nIf the mayor of Ankradem decides to kill 3,000 people, nobody will die because the city doesn't exist. If anyone were to die, the death would be really painful though.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"attChk.text","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In Ankradem, there are some experimenters who would like to make sure that you are still reading...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID3610","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},
