{"SurveyID":"SV_2t4UF1nJSAUJ3My","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4311","SecondaryAttribute":"Toxic factory A fire in a chemical factory threatens to release heptahopretyde, a gas that kills...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Toxic factory<\/b><br><br>\n\nA fire in a chemical factory threatens to release heptahopretyde, a gas that kills within seconds even in minimal doses. If released, everybody in the immediately surrounding area will be killed, though the factory workers themselves will be fine due to their respiratory equipment.\n<br> <br>\nThe firefighters can prevent the release of heptahopretyde by using heavy lift helicopters to drop a containment tent over the building that concentrates and then purifies the gases. This will save 400 people in the surrounding area. However, this will overwhelm the respiratory equipment of 300 workers in the factory and will kill them due to heptahopretyde exposure.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.toxicFactory.neutral.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.400.n_total.700.n_victims.300.ratio_saved_victims.1.333333333.text","QuestionID":"QID4311","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Toxic factory A fire in a chemical factory threatens to release heptahopretyde, a gas that kills...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
